{
  "id": "V09",
  "title": "Offset stack with and without a post",
  "intent": "An upper wall (x = 4–12 ft) sits on a longer wall below (0–16 ft), so both upper ends land mid-wall. Tool rule: a wall end transfers only where it aligns with a wall end below (±0.1 ft); a mid-wall end needs a post. Line A has no post: warning, nothing is transferred, the lower wall is designed for its own load only. Line B adds a post under each upper end: the post carries the end force to the foundation (base holdown, post member for max(ASD, Ω₀ ASD)) and the lower wall is still unchanged.",
  "covers": [
    "Wall end transfer rule (aligned ends only)",
    "Mid-wall end → warning, no transfer",
    "Support post at any story",
    "Post base HDUE",
    "Support post member max(ASD, Ω₀ ASD) (ASCE 7-22 §12.3.3.3)"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Both lines: Roof V_T = 2 k (upper wall, L = 8 ft, h = 9 ft); Level 1 V_B = 5 k (lower wall, L = 16 ft, h = 10 ft). Self-weight only (10 psf)."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Upper wall: v = 0.7 × 2000 / 8 = 175.00 plf → 6\" o.c.. D = 10 × 8 × 9 = 0.72 k → R = 0.36 k; N_E = 2 × 9 / 8 = ±2.250 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Upper wall ends: T = 0.7 × 2.250 − 0.46 × 0.36 = 1.409 k; C = 1.14 × 0.36 + 0.7 × 2.250 = 1.985 k (same at both ends by symmetry)."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Lower wall (own load only): v = 0.7 × 5000 / 16 = 218.75 plf → 6\" o.c.. D = 10 × 16 × 10 = 1.60 k → R = 0.80 k; N_E = 5 × 10 / 16 = ±3.125 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Lower wall: T = 0.7 × 3.125 − 0.46 × 0.80 = 1.820 k → HDUE3; C = 1.14 × 0.80 + 0.7 × 3.125 = 3.099 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Line A: upper ends at x = 4 and 12 land inside the lower wall (0–16), no post → warning \"add a post below\", no transfer: the lower wall keeps T = 1.820 / C = 3.099 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Line B: posts P-B1 (x = 4) and P-B2 (x = 12) in the Level 1 story each receive one upper end: envelope T = 1.409 k, C = 1.985 k. The lower wall is unchanged (T = 1.820 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Post base at the foundation: T = 1.409 k → HDUE3. Post member: Ω₀ ASD (5) = 1.14 × 0.36 + 0.7 × 2.5 × 2.250 = 4.348 k > ASD 1.985 k → design C = 4.348 k → (2)2x4 at 10 ft (cap 5.00 k, HDUE3 minimum (2)2x4)."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Checks: Line A loses the upper end forces (listed by the audit, excluded, not failed); Line B carries everything to the foundation → G1–G12 pass on both lines."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Upper wall (both lines) — SW-A1 / SW-B1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 2.000 / 8 = 250.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0102; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1406; Δ_HD = 0.0808 × 2250.00 / 1535/0.7 = 0.0829 (MSTC28, T = 2250.00 lb); r = 2250.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.3429 → Δ_c = 0.0094; h·Δa/b = 9 × (0.0829 + 0.0094) / 8 = 0.1038 → δ = 0.2547 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "Lower wall (both lines; no end force from above: Line A no post, Line B on the posts) — SW-A2 / SW-B2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 5.000 / 16 = 312.50 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0088; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1953; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 3125.00 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.1047 (HDUE3, T = 3125.00 lb); r = 3125.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.4762 → Δ_c = 0.0130; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1047 + 0.0130) / 16 = 0.0736 → δ = 0.2777 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 12,
      "text": "Both lines: Story drift Roof: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-A1 / SW-B1 0.2547 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2547 / 1.0 = 1.019 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 13,
      "text": "Both lines: Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-A2 / SW-B2 0.2777 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2777 / 1.0 = 1.111 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
